# Generated from: specs/561-default-the-execute-implement-stage-to-opus-at-medium-effort-and-offer-the-new-defaults-on-upgrade/requirements.md
Feature: Default the execute implement stage to Opus at medium effort

  @SCN001
  Scenario: New plugin defaults
    Given the plugin stage defaults
    Then implement is opus at medium effort and verify is opus at high effort

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Onboarding and upgrade write the new defaults
    Given a project without steering/sdlc-models.json
    When onboarding or upgrade creates it
    Then it holds the new defaults

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Upgrade offers the new defaults to a project on the old ones
    Given a complete stage models file whose implement entry is haiku at xhigh
    When upgrade runs
    Then it offers an sdlc-models-defaults item for implement
    And approving it sets implement to opus at medium and keeps every other value
    And a custom implement entry is never offered

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Docs and this repository match
    Given the README and this repository's stage models file
    Then they state the new defaults
